<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Entitlements for the REAL protected helper inside
         Resources/bin/TypeProtectedGigaAM.app (assembled by afterPack.js). It
         stores its Secure Enclave key references and wrapped-CEK cache in the
         Data Protection Keychain, which macOS only grants to a process that has
         an application identifier authorized by an embedded provisioning
         profile. Without these SecKeyCreateRandomKey fails with
         errSecMissingEntitlement (-34018).

         The team prefix (SBHVKH5UUY) and identifier MUST match the signer's
         Developer ID + provisioning profile. Current signer: Mikhail Naer
         (SBHVKH5UUY), profile application-identifier SBHVKH5UUY.ai.gigatype.app,
         keychain-access-groups SBHVKH5UUY.*. If a different team signs, update
         all three strings to that team's <TEAMID>.ai.gigatype.app.

         model_identity.rs sets no explicit kSecAttrAccessGroup, so the key lands
         in the default group = this application-identifier — which is why the
         nested bundle's id matches the outer app (ai.gigatype.app). -->
    <key>com.apple.application-identifier</key>
    <string>SBHVKH5UUY.ai.gigatype.app</string>
    <key>com.apple.developer.team-identifier</key>
    <string>SBHVKH5UUY</string>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>SBHVKH5UUY.ai.gigatype.app</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
